# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true gives Windows clones CRLF working copies.
# Prettier writes LF, so it would then report every file as unformatted, and
# the pre-commit hook would rewrite whatever it touched — churn in each commit
# that has nothing to do with the change being made.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are Git's to detect, but naming them keeps that decision explicit
# for the ones actually in the tree.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
